<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conchobar mac Nessa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Conchobar mac Nessa is the legendary king of the Ulaid in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulster-cycle">Ulster Cycle</a> of Irish literature, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emain-macha">Emain Macha</a>. He appears in the Táin Bó Cúailnge and in the tragic tale of Deirdre, whom he sought to marry. Medieval tradition placed his reign around the time of Christ.</p></div>
